{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03439",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 7.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Right, hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.7,
      "end_seconds": 12.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Erm, hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.65,
      "end_seconds": 19.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.25,
      "end_seconds": 30.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "So, um, I've been coughing up large amounts of blood, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.93,
      "end_seconds": 34.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.66,
      "end_seconds": 46.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "It's been about three months, I'm fairly sure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.96,
      "end_seconds": 57.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.72,
      "end_seconds": 69.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Hmm, it happens once or twice a day. I'd give it a seven, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.92,
      "end_seconds": 72.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "What about breathlessness, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.94,
      "end_seconds": 78.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.86,
      "end_seconds": 86.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Have you been feeling faint?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.36,
      "end_seconds": 94.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Yes, since last night. As for feeling faint, I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.26,
      "end_seconds": 99.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Alright, tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.36,
      "end_seconds": 115.58,
      "duration_seconds": 15.22,
      "text": "It's, It's fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning. Actually, it's propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day for the migraine prevention. Okay, so before this I was on escitalopram; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.43,
      "end_seconds": 119.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.35,
      "end_seconds": 124.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Yes, I had my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.49,
      "end_seconds": 128.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.68,
      "end_seconds": 133.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Yes, depression. Migraines, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.63,
      "end_seconds": 142.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.54,
      "end_seconds": 146.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.62,
      "end_seconds": 154.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.78,
      "end_seconds": 159.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.84,
      "end_seconds": 163.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.31,
      "end_seconds": 168.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Walnuts. I come out in... well, my lips swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.13,
      "end_seconds": 189.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "And what about weight loss or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.14,
      "end_seconds": 193.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.48,
      "end_seconds": 198.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.4,
      "end_seconds": 201.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Definitely no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.02,
      "end_seconds": 204.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.57,
      "end_seconds": 210.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Okay, so that's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.01,
      "end_seconds": 231.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.39,
      "end_seconds": 242.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.29,
      "end_seconds": 267.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 93, BP is 134 over 89. And SpO2 89 percent on room air, respiratory rate 26."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.46,
      "end_seconds": 270.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.26,
      "end_seconds": 275.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.0,
      "end_seconds": 281.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.51,
      "end_seconds": 284.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.1,
      "end_seconds": 301.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "You are pale, breathing fast and bringing up fresh blood with every cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.26,
      "end_seconds": 316.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Alright, thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards life-threatening haemoptysis. I'd also keep a pulmonary embolus in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.47,
      "end_seconds": 322.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Oh, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.22,
      "end_seconds": 336.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now life-threatening haemoptysis is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'm sending you for urgent blood tests because of bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 337.71,
      "end_seconds": 341.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "We have a slot Thursday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.65,
      "end_seconds": 348.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay, I'll be there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.94,
      "end_seconds": 377.86,
      "duration_seconds": 27.92,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an urgent CT scan because of massive haemoptysis. What I'm giving you is tranexamic acid, 1 gram, now, single dose. It's for haemoptysis. Lie on the bleeding side and I am calling the emergency team. The emergency team would be the right next step, I'll refer you. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.23,
      "end_seconds": 386.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.23,
      "end_seconds": 395.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "So, I take the tranexamic acid, 1 gram, now. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.95,
      "end_seconds": 401.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.05,
      "end_seconds": 406.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}